WEBVTT

00:00:05.480 --> 00:00:08.020
Yakumo-kun, here...

00:00:26.880 --> 00:00:28.290
Thank you.

00:00:31.550 --> 00:00:33.800
You finally spoke.

00:00:37.760 --> 00:00:40.810
He's registered as a donor.

00:00:40.810 --> 00:00:43.310
You mean an organ donor?

00:00:43.890 --> 00:00:48.860
They'll start harvesting his organs as soon as I, his next of kin, consent.

00:00:48.860 --> 00:00:51.320
So did you consent to it?

00:00:52.190 --> 00:00:58.620
I can't see his ghost with my left eye, so I didn't consent to it.

00:00:59.200 --> 00:01:00.990
That's right.

00:01:00.990 --> 00:01:04.330
He looks like he's just sleeping.

00:01:05.210 --> 00:01:09.840
I... those people who left my uncle in this condition...

00:01:11.210 --> 00:01:12.590
I hate them.

00:01:13.840 --> 00:01:15.590
Yakumo-kun...

00:01:24.480 --> 00:01:25.390
That's...

00:01:50.630 --> 00:01:51.670
What's the matter?

00:02:01.300 --> 00:02:02.970
I couldn't see her face,

00:02:02.970 --> 00:02:08.520
but judging from her height and stature, I'm positive we just saw her.

00:02:08.520 --> 00:02:11.560
But she's still alive...

00:02:12.770 --> 00:02:14.780
Please keep this a secret, but...

00:02:15.400 --> 00:02:19.410
unless she undergoes an organ transplant, she only has six months left.

00:02:19.410 --> 00:02:20.200
What?

00:02:23.160 --> 00:02:27.200
Her attending physician, Doctor Sakakibara, tried everything he could, but...

00:02:27.200 --> 00:02:29.040
Nothing worked.

00:02:29.710 --> 00:02:33.210
When I imagine what Doctor Sakakibara's going through... It must hurt so much...

00:02:33.960 --> 00:02:35.840
Because Yoshiko-chan is his-

00:02:36.920 --> 00:02:39.470
No, it's nothing.

00:02:48.850 --> 00:02:50.690
Hey, did you find something?

00:02:54.480 --> 00:02:56.900
Y-Yakumo-kun?

00:03:25.430 --> 00:03:27.810
That's definitely the missing ambulance.

00:03:28.270 --> 00:03:31.810
The suspect it was carrying may still be hiding somewhere nearby.

00:03:31.810 --> 00:03:33.270
Be careful.

00:03:33.650 --> 00:03:35.810
Perfect timing.

00:03:37.020 --> 00:03:38.110
You're...

00:03:40.280 --> 00:03:41.740
Don't move.

00:04:03.760 --> 00:04:06.260
Yakumo identified the real culprit?

00:04:06.550 --> 00:04:10.270
So, the culprit isn't his father?

00:04:10.270 --> 00:04:12.140
I think so.

00:04:12.140 --> 00:04:15.230
Yakumo-kun refuses to talk to me.

00:04:15.230 --> 00:04:17.610
So he hasn't told you either, huh?

00:04:17.610 --> 00:04:19.940
That's nothing unusual though.

00:04:19.940 --> 00:04:23.780
But somehow he seems different from his usual self.

00:04:23.780 --> 00:04:25.200
What?

00:04:25.200 --> 00:04:29.330
I believe it's because of what's happened to Isshin-san.

00:04:29.330 --> 00:04:31.870
The manifestation of hatred...

00:04:31.870 --> 00:04:35.000
I get the feeling that he hates the entire world right now.

00:04:37.880 --> 00:04:40.130
That sounds exactly like how he was in middle school.

00:04:40.500 --> 00:04:45.050
Goto-san, you knew him when he was in middle school?

00:04:45.050 --> 00:04:46.590
Yeah...

00:04:46.590 --> 00:04:48.100
Can you please tell me what he was like?

00:04:48.100 --> 00:04:49.010
What?

00:04:49.430 --> 00:04:52.270
I'm not asking out of curiosity.

00:04:53.560 --> 00:04:56.350
I'm worried about him.

00:04:56.900 --> 00:04:58.520
So...

00:05:04.820 --> 00:05:07.870
It'll be troublesome, but I guess I can.

00:05:07.870 --> 00:05:14.000
Yakumo always says that my stories are hard to follow and jump around all over the place,

00:05:14.000 --> 00:05:17.540
so it might be long, but I'll start right from the very beginning.

00:05:18.130 --> 00:05:19.420
Please do.

00:05:23.800 --> 00:05:31.850
I first met him the night I stopped his mother from killing him.

00:05:31.850 --> 00:05:34.930
That was when I learned his name was Yakumo.

00:05:35.890 --> 00:05:39.060
However, I didn't see him after that night...

00:05:40.360 --> 00:05:42.270
Until a few years later...

00:05:44.740 --> 00:05:49.660
I was investigating a case and it was by sheer coincidence that I met Yakumo again.

00:05:51.660 --> 00:05:54.120
Damn it! Where did that bastard go?

00:06:01.000 --> 00:06:04.840
Hey, kid, what are you doing out here so late?

00:06:05.670 --> 00:06:07.340
Killing time.

00:06:07.340 --> 00:06:08.380
What?

00:06:09.180 --> 00:06:12.350
It's too late for kids to be wandering around outside.

00:06:12.850 --> 00:06:14.850
It's none of your business.

00:06:15.430 --> 00:06:16.810
I'm with the police.

00:06:16.810 --> 00:06:17.890
I know.

00:06:17.890 --> 00:06:18.640
What?

00:06:18.640 --> 00:06:20.350
You're annoying.

00:06:20.350 --> 00:06:23.440
You really think you can frighten everyone by just flashing your badge around?

00:06:23.440 --> 00:06:24.570
Rather simple-minded of you.

00:06:24.570 --> 00:06:25.860
What did you just say?!

00:06:25.860 --> 00:06:27.360
Hey, what's your name?

00:06:27.860 --> 00:06:29.570
I've told you before.

00:06:29.570 --> 00:06:31.120
I don't know you-

00:06:31.660 --> 00:06:38.120
I'm surprised you can do your job as a police officer considering the poor memory you have, Officer Goto.

00:06:38.870 --> 00:06:40.870
How do you know my name?

00:06:44.750 --> 00:06:50.380
It was only later that I discovered that kid was Yakumo.

00:06:58.520 --> 00:07:01.270
Hey! What are you kids doing?!

00:07:02.730 --> 00:07:03.520
Oh no!

00:07:04.230 --> 00:07:05.520
Are you all right?

00:07:09.530 --> 00:07:12.280
You're from that park the other day.

00:07:13.030 --> 00:07:14.280
Perfect.

00:07:14.280 --> 00:07:16.540
I have a load of questions for you.

00:07:16.950 --> 00:07:19.290
I've got nothing to say to you.

00:07:20.250 --> 00:07:23.040
Stop acting tough, you brat!

00:07:27.630 --> 00:07:28.840
That eye...

00:07:34.260 --> 00:07:35.220
You're...

00:07:36.010 --> 00:07:39.520
Don't tell me... from back then?

00:07:39.930 --> 00:07:42.020
Hey! Are you all right?

00:07:51.900 --> 00:07:57.030
And then with a devilish expression he asked:

00:07:57.910 --> 00:08:03.540
"Why did you bother saving me when my own mother was trying to kill me?"

00:08:03.540 --> 00:08:06.040
Yakumo-kun asked that?

00:08:06.420 --> 00:08:12.260
He then told me that he didn't ask to be rescued.

00:08:12.260 --> 00:08:20.060
But back then, he didn't know the real reason behind why his mother tried to kill him, right?

00:08:20.060 --> 00:08:22.430
I punched him.

00:08:22.430 --> 00:08:26.270
"What's wrong with saving a life that's about to end right in front of me?"

00:08:26.270 --> 00:08:28.070
That was all I could think...

00:08:28.570 --> 00:08:32.650
I had him pinned down before I realized it.

00:08:37.620 --> 00:08:42.250
Since then, our unsavory ties have continued.

00:08:42.250 --> 00:08:44.830
You know, he's changed a lot since then.

00:08:45.250 --> 00:08:48.670
Although I know he'll deny it with every breath he's got,

00:08:48.670 --> 00:08:51.920
I think you were the one who changed him.

00:08:52.380 --> 00:08:53.970
I was?

00:08:53.970 --> 00:08:55.130
That's right.

00:08:55.130 --> 00:09:00.430
However, with Isshin ending up like he is, I think he...

00:09:01.390 --> 00:09:04.430
He's reverting back to his old self...

00:09:04.430 --> 00:09:05.440
No way!

00:09:05.440 --> 00:09:10.570
I don't want to see him like that either... ever again.

00:09:11.020 --> 00:09:13.440
D-Detective Goto, it's an emergency!

00:09:14.030 --> 00:09:15.070
What's wrong?

00:09:15.070 --> 00:09:18.120
Nanase Miyuki's escaped!

00:09:18.120 --> 00:09:19.280
What?!

00:09:19.280 --> 00:09:22.490
Two officers have died in the line of duty and a gun was stolen.

00:09:26.120 --> 00:09:27.040
Who's this?!

00:09:27.460 --> 00:09:29.080
Oh, it's you.

00:09:29.630 --> 00:09:32.000
I'm visiting Isshin-san with Nao-chan.

00:09:32.000 --> 00:09:34.300
I think we'll be home late tonight-

00:09:34.300 --> 00:09:36.840
Oh, Nao-chan, where are you going?

00:09:38.090 --> 00:09:39.600
Oh, Nao-chan.

00:09:40.800 --> 00:09:42.100
Hello.

00:10:02.740 --> 00:10:03.830
What?

00:10:03.830 --> 00:10:06.620
Oh, it's you. The lady from the press.

00:10:07.080 --> 00:10:08.870
What? You saw Yakumo?

00:10:08.870 --> 00:10:09.750
At the hospital?

00:10:12.340 --> 00:10:15.760
He was acting strange.

00:10:15.760 --> 00:10:19.510
It didn't seem like he was here to visit Isshin-san.

00:10:20.260 --> 00:10:21.760
That bastard Yakumo.

00:10:21.760 --> 00:10:23.350
What's he planning?

00:10:23.350 --> 00:10:24.770
Goto-san?

00:10:24.770 --> 00:10:26.310
Send a car over right away.

00:10:26.310 --> 00:10:27.270
Yes, sir!

00:10:29.100 --> 00:10:34.190
Are you saying I purposely left your uncle brain dead?

00:10:34.570 --> 00:10:39.030
While it's true that I promote organ donation,

00:10:39.570 --> 00:10:44.950
I would never do something like that.

00:10:44.950 --> 00:10:48.460
It's no use lying, Doctor Sakakibara.

00:10:48.460 --> 00:10:51.460
The law accepts that being brain dead is the same as being dead.

00:10:51.920 --> 00:10:55.960
What you've carried out is nothing other than a planned murder.

00:11:12.270 --> 00:11:13.610
Huh?

00:11:17.860 --> 00:11:20.740
I can see the souls of the dead,

00:11:21.610 --> 00:11:26.540
and very rarely, I can detect another type of soul,

00:11:26.990 --> 00:11:28.160
a living ghost.

00:11:28.910 --> 00:11:34.130
It's possible for a soul to leave its own body while it's still alive when it has a strong desire.

00:11:34.750 --> 00:11:40.130
In her case, her soul may naturally be predisposed to leaving her body.

00:11:40.760 --> 00:11:45.430
Every night, her soul has appeared in front of the hospitalized patients,

00:11:45.430 --> 00:11:48.020
and asked them when they will die.

00:11:48.640 --> 00:11:52.690
That's because you, her attending physician, told her that unless she undergoes an organ transplant,

00:11:53.270 --> 00:11:56.440
she'll only have six months left to live.

00:11:56.440 --> 00:11:59.650
So now you're telling ghost stories to physicians?

00:11:59.650 --> 00:12:04.950
"If a patient dies, their organs can be transplanted into me, and I will live."

00:12:05.530 --> 00:12:09.790
This strong desire subconsciously allowed the phenomenon

00:12:09.790 --> 00:12:12.580
of a soul leaving a living body to occur.

00:12:13.210 --> 00:12:15.710
Her name is Mamiya Yoshiko.

00:12:16.460 --> 00:12:20.670
Doctor Sakakibara, she's your daughter.

00:12:24.470 --> 00:12:29.430
I became suspicious because of something Doctor Arai said, so I investigated your background.

00:12:29.970 --> 00:12:32.520
You're divorced.

00:12:32.520 --> 00:12:34.770
Your wife took custody of your daughter,

00:12:34.770 --> 00:12:37.690
and your daughter went by her mother's maiden name, Mamiya.

00:12:45.700 --> 00:12:48.330
She's my own flesh and blood after all.

00:12:48.330 --> 00:12:53.460
I didn't want the other patients to misunderstand, so I kept it a secret. That's all there is.

00:12:53.460 --> 00:12:55.080
This conversation is now finished.

00:12:57.790 --> 00:12:59.920
However, this is what I think really happened...

00:13:00.460 --> 00:13:03.760
You discovered that my uncle was registered as an organ donor

00:13:03.760 --> 00:13:06.300
when he came in for a complete checkup,

00:13:06.300 --> 00:13:09.260
so you secretly investigated whether he was a match to your daughter.

00:13:09.970 --> 00:13:12.310
The results were a perfect match.

00:13:12.310 --> 00:13:17.980
Furthermore, you investigated the criteria used to determine an organ recipient...

00:13:17.980 --> 00:13:22.320
In other words, the medical urgency, the waiting period, cold ischemic time...

00:13:22.320 --> 00:13:24.740
After you had personally verified every criterion required for an organ transplant,

00:13:24.740 --> 00:13:29.570
you became 100% certain that my uncle's organs would be transplanted to Yoshiko-chan.

00:13:32.330 --> 00:13:35.000
However, my uncle was expected to live for a year.

00:13:35.000 --> 00:13:39.630
It would be too late if you waited for him to die, and that's why...

00:13:47.470 --> 00:13:52.640
After you stabbed my uncle, you rushed back to the hospital.

00:13:55.390 --> 00:13:58.230
You needed to ensure that you met my uncle as the doctor on night duty,

00:13:58.230 --> 00:14:00.480
so that you could be certain he ended up brain dead.

00:14:00.860 --> 00:14:02.860
Enough.

00:14:02.860 --> 00:14:04.900
I need to leave straightaway.

00:14:04.900 --> 00:14:06.280
Don't get in my way.

00:14:10.280 --> 00:14:11.780
What happened here?

00:14:12.620 --> 00:14:14.580
I-I hit it in my garage at home-

00:14:14.580 --> 00:14:15.790
You're lying.

00:14:15.790 --> 00:14:22.920
This was damaged when you hit an oncoming car while racing back to the hospital.

00:14:22.920 --> 00:14:24.840
And what are you basing this on?

00:14:25.590 --> 00:14:28.380
I was the driver of the car you hit.

00:14:36.850 --> 00:14:38.890
But what can this damage prove?

00:14:38.890 --> 00:14:42.480
Besides, most of your deductions are based on pure speculation.

00:14:42.480 --> 00:14:44.860
If you plan to denounce me, a respected physician,

00:14:44.860 --> 00:14:47.400
I suggest you prove I've committed medical malpractice first!

00:14:47.690 --> 00:14:50.530
Besides, aren't you forgetting that the murder was foretold?

00:14:50.530 --> 00:14:54.450
Of the two fugitives, one was arrested and foretold that Isshin's murder would take place!

00:14:54.450 --> 00:14:58.160
Why do you even suspect me? That's just wrong!

00:14:58.580 --> 00:15:02.670
What you said just now <i>is</i> proof that you did it.

00:15:03.500 --> 00:15:04.920
What do you mean by that?

00:15:04.920 --> 00:15:11.640
The police never released the fact that this attempted murder was foretold.

00:15:11.970 --> 00:15:13.850
Wh-What?!

00:15:13.850 --> 00:15:22.850
The only ones who know aside from the police are those around me and the culprit himself.

00:15:30.570 --> 00:15:31.860
Who are you?

00:15:37.410 --> 00:15:39.160
It's a detective I know.

00:15:44.460 --> 00:15:45.750
Oh?

00:15:47.920 --> 00:15:49.510
Wait, you!

00:15:49.510 --> 00:15:51.050
Why are you going after him?

00:15:51.050 --> 00:15:55.050
Obviously, because he's running away!

00:16:06.820 --> 00:16:11.570
A hospital this big is bound to have helicopter facilities.

00:16:11.860 --> 00:16:15.570
If you can't escape by car, then this is your only option.

00:16:15.570 --> 00:16:17.370
However, it's useless.

00:16:17.370 --> 00:16:22.080
No matter what reason you give, no helicopters can fly in this weather.

00:16:22.080 --> 00:16:23.870
There's nowhere left to run.

00:16:25.750 --> 00:16:28.460
How old will your uncle be this year?

00:16:28.920 --> 00:16:32.090
My daughter's only twelve!

00:16:33.170 --> 00:16:35.840
She's only lived for twelve years.

00:16:38.810 --> 00:16:41.220
He'll die within a year anyway.

00:16:41.220 --> 00:16:43.440
What's wrong with killing him earlier and saving my daughter?

00:16:44.810 --> 00:16:47.360
Saving a life that can be saved?!

00:16:47.360 --> 00:16:51.360
That doesn't give you the right to take someone's life away!

00:16:51.780 --> 00:16:53.030
Yes, it does!

00:16:53.860 --> 00:16:56.870
If it'll save Yoshiko, then I'll...

00:16:57.820 --> 00:16:59.370
I'll...

00:17:21.310 --> 00:17:24.140
Humans are completely foolish,

00:17:24.640 --> 00:17:28.060
don't you think, Yakumo?

00:17:35.530 --> 00:17:38.240
That idiot Yakumo! Where did he disappear to?

00:17:38.240 --> 00:17:41.030
The only place we haven't checked is...

00:17:41.620 --> 00:17:44.830
Has anyone checked the roof?

00:17:44.830 --> 00:17:46.410
I haven't.

00:17:46.410 --> 00:17:48.040
Neither have I.

00:17:50.040 --> 00:17:51.380
Nao-chan?

00:17:52.710 --> 00:17:54.800
What? You want to come too?

00:17:54.800 --> 00:17:57.840
Now, Nao-chan, don't bother everyone, okay?

00:18:00.760 --> 00:18:02.310
Nao-chan.

00:18:02.310 --> 00:18:05.480
You're worried about Yakumo-kun, aren't you?

00:18:08.310 --> 00:18:09.770
You can come with us.

00:18:10.860 --> 00:18:12.980
But dear...

00:18:12.980 --> 00:18:14.860
Wait for us in the lobby.

00:18:14.860 --> 00:18:16.820
I'm a police officer after all.

00:18:17.860 --> 00:18:19.570
I'll protect her.

00:18:21.700 --> 00:18:24.580
The love between a parent and their child is precious.

00:18:25.040 --> 00:18:32.090
They think nothing of killing another, so that their child can live on.

00:18:32.090 --> 00:18:38.090
That's the truth behind the humans which you believe in, Yakumo.

00:18:38.090 --> 00:18:41.590
So, you're the one who encouraged Doctor Sakakibara.

00:18:41.590 --> 00:18:43.600
Encouraged?

00:18:43.600 --> 00:18:49.100
That's not true. I merely presented him with an opportunity.

00:18:50.690 --> 00:18:54.110
Are you saying that you'll take all the blame?

00:18:54.400 --> 00:18:55.480
That's right.

00:18:56.150 --> 00:19:01.990
My only concern is for the death of a man named Saito Isshin.

00:19:01.990 --> 00:19:10.120
However, if I kill him, I may damage the organ your daughter requires.

00:19:10.460 --> 00:19:13.630
So that's why you're telling me to...

00:19:13.920 --> 00:19:19.260
H-However, as a physician, that is-

00:19:19.260 --> 00:19:23.010
Feeling the pangs of conscience, perhaps? Or is this your physician's morals?

00:19:23.010 --> 00:19:25.640
I care nothing for such values.

00:19:26.010 --> 00:19:32.150
Sakakibara-san, the truth behind humans is darkness.

00:19:40.150 --> 00:19:43.030
I can feel it, Yakumo...

00:19:43.030 --> 00:19:46.200
Your strong hatred!

00:19:55.670 --> 00:19:56.920
Yakumo-kun!

00:19:56.920 --> 00:19:57.630
Wait!

00:20:02.800 --> 00:20:05.050
I like the look of those eyes.

00:20:05.050 --> 00:20:07.930
You're truly my son.

00:20:13.020 --> 00:20:15.520
What's he doing?

00:20:21.780 --> 00:20:23.700
Just as I suspected.

00:20:24.740 --> 00:20:26.530
You are...

00:20:31.830 --> 00:20:33.790
a ghost.

00:20:38.090 --> 00:20:42.170
A ghost is a cluster of emotions.

00:20:42.170 --> 00:20:47.300
Yakumo, can you see the root of my emotions?

00:20:50.560 --> 00:20:52.980
Despair and enmity.

00:20:52.980 --> 00:20:56.060
They are what shape me.

00:20:56.440 --> 00:21:01.940
Just like you... now that you have lost Isshin.

00:21:02.990 --> 00:21:05.070
However, Yakumo,

00:21:05.780 --> 00:21:06.950
it's not over.

00:21:08.240 --> 00:21:10.160
Not yet.
